# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Work only on the current phase. The current phase is Phase 5. See [docs/phase-5.md](docs/phase-5.md). Phase 1, Phase 2, Phase 3, and Phase 4 are complete.

Feature work happens on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 5 is trading accounts. Paper accounts still use the Phase 4 paper ledger. Do not place exchange orders. Do not add encrypted exchange keys or a Fly.io worker. Do not call Bybit from the browser. Live accounts may exist; the tick must not execute them.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture.

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Work one micro-step at a time as listed in [docs/phase-5.md](docs/phase-5.md). Stop at the end of each micro-step and wait for instruction.

Stop at the end of the phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
